The issue is that in the test environment, `Account.Name` is a required text field (not a formula), so inserting an Account without a `Name` fails. In a real NPSP org the Name field is a formula on the Household RT and auto-computes, but the test doesn't have that.

The fix: provide a bootstrap value for `Name` (the first member's last name) so the insert succeeds. In a real NPSP org the naming formula/trigger immediately overwrites it — we're not constructing the NPSP household-name format, just satisfying the platform's required-field validation so the record can be created at all.

