The issue is that `npsp.TDTM_Runnable.Action` doesn't have enum members named `AFTER_INSERT`/`AFTER_UPDATE`. I'll fix this by determining the trigger context from the `oldlist` parameter (empty/null = insert, populated = update), which is how the TDTM framework actually communicates context and avoids depending on specific enum constant names.

File: force-app/main/default/classes/OPP_MajorGiftFollowUp_TDTM.cls
```apex
public class OPP_MajorGiftFollowUp_TDTM extends npsp.TDTM_Runnable {

    public OPP_MajorGiftFollowUp_TDTM() {
        // No-arg constructor required for TDTM reflection-based instantiation
    }

    public override npsp.TDTM_Runnable.DmlWrapper run(
        List<SObject> newlist,
        List<SObject> oldlist,
        npsp.TDTM_Runnable.Action triggerAction,
        Schema.DescribeSObjectResult objResult
    ) {
        List<Task> tasks = new List<Task>();

        if (oldlist == null || oldlist.isEmpty()) {
            // INSERT context: no prior state exists
            for (SObject sobj : newlist) {
                Opportunity opp = (Opportunity) sobj;
                if (isQualifying(opp)) {
                    tasks.add(buildTask(opp));
                }
            }
        } else {
            // UPDATE context: compare old and new state
            for (Integer i = 0; i < newlist.size(); i++) {
                Opportunity newOpp = (Opportunity) newlist[i];
                Opportunity oldOpp = (Opportunity) oldlist[i];
                if (isQualifying(newOpp) && !isQualifying(oldOpp)) {
                    tasks.add(buildTask(newOpp));
                }
            }
        }

        if (!tasks.isEmpty()) {
            insert tasks;
        }

        return null;
    }

    private Boolean isQualifying(Opportunity opp) {
        return opp.StageName == 'Closed Won'
            && opp.Amount != null
            && opp.Amount >= 5000;
    }

    private Task buildTask(Opportunity opp) {
        return new Task(
            Subject = 'Major gift thank-you call',
            Priority = 'High',
            Status = 'Not Started',
            WhatId = opp.Id,
            WhoId = opp.npsp__Primary_Contact__c,
            OwnerId = opp.OwnerId,
            ActivityDate = opp.CloseDate != null ? opp.CloseDate.addDays(3) : null
        );
    }
}
```

**What changed and why:**

| Before (broken) | After (fixed) | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| `triggerAction == npsp.TDTM_Runnable.Action.AFTER_INSERT` | `oldlist == null \|\| oldlist.isEmpty()` | The enum constants `AFTER_INSERT`/`AFTER_UPDATE` don't exist in this NPSP version. The TDTM framework passes an empty list for `oldlist` on inserts and a populated list on updates, so we derive context from that. |
| `triggerAction == npsp.TDTM_Runnable.Action.AFTER_UPDATE` | `else` branch (oldlist is populated) | Same reasoning — if `oldlist` has records, it's an update context. |

This approach is actually more robust because it doesn't couple the handler to specific enum member names, and the insert/update distinction via `oldlist` emptiness is the same contract Salesforce guarantees for `Trigger.old`.

